     "\r<br>On Wed, May 13, 2009 at 8:53 PM, JiHO &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jo.l...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; On 2009-May-13  , at 19:32 , David Kahle wrote:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; ## manually calculate the lines where you want them\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; dens &lt;- kde2d(df$X1, df$X2, n = 100)\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; sorry for my first reply which overlooked the tiny problem that you\r<br>&gt; can&#39;t have two stats for one geom. So David is correct, you have to\r<br>&gt; compute the density outside of ggplot. However, once you do that,\r<br>&gt; there is no need to do all the rest manually too. You can use\r<br>&gt; geom_contour directly. See the second example in stat_density2d or :\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; library(&quot;ggplot2&quot;)\r<br>&gt; library(&quot;MASS&quot;)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; d = data.frame(x=rnorm(1000),y=rnorm(1000))\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; dens = MASS::kde2d(d$x, d$y, n = 100)\r<br>&gt; densf = data.frame(expand.grid(x=dens$x, y=dens$y), z=as.vector(dens$z))\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; ggplot(densf, aes(x=x,y=y,z=z)) + geom_contour(breaks=seq(min(densf\r<br>&gt; $z), max(densf$z), length.out=10))\r<br>&gt; # this puts 10 equally spaced breaks but you could put whatever you\r<br>&gt; want in the breaks parameter\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I hope this is more helpful.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; JiHO\r<br>&gt; ---\r<br>&gt; <a href=\"http://jo.irisson.free.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://jo.irisson.free.fr/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792386032701000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2YZFmXvgcUli1qkH8ZiYz5\">http://jo.irisson.free.fr/</a>\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; &gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>"
